<section id="method" class="v2-section v2-method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <header class="v2-section__header"><div><p>HOW TO READ THE SIGNAL</p><h2 id="method-title">Methodology</h2></div><span>CONTRACT V2.2.0</span></header>
  <div class="v2-method__grid">
    <article><span>01 / SOURCES</span><h3>Keep article and community separate.</h3><p>Article analysis measures the source&rsquo;s adopted claims. Community analysis measures visible HN discussion at collection time. Neither is public opinion or ground truth.</p></article>
    <article><span>02 / DIMENSIONS</span><h3>One verdict is not enough.</h3><p>Capability tracks present usefulness. Trajectory tracks expected change. Impact tracks consequences for people and institutions. Missing evidence is never converted to neutral.</p></article>
    <article><span>03 / WEIGHT</span><h3>Confidence changes influence, not direction.</h3><p>Combined dimensions use 40% article and 60% community priors, multiplied by source confidence. Disagreement and polarization remain diagnostics rather than confidence penalties.</p></article>
    <article><span>04 / LIMITS</span><h3>Tension stays visible.</h3><p>Source divergence, effective sample size, branch spread, ranking sensitivity and exact evidence remain inspectable. Generated comment summaries are labeled as summaries, never quotes.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>
